WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.765
Sun angle determines where light and shadow fall.

00:00:02.765 --> 00:00:05.089
Low sun can produce long shadows that hide features,

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:08.229
while direct sun can create glare and wash out reflective surfaces.

00:00:08.229 --> 00:00:11.818
Backlighting can make an obstacle or aircraft silhouette difficult to see.

00:00:11.818 --> 00:00:14.398
Lighting changes during a mission and across repeat flights.

00:00:14.398 --> 00:00:18.487
Before-and-after imagery collected at different times may show shadow differences that

00:00:18.487 --> 00:00:19.827
resemble structural change.

00:00:19.827 --> 00:00:23.542
Record capture time and conditions so analysts can separate illumination from scene

00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:24.052
change.

00:00:24.052 --> 00:00:27.876
Low-light conditions increase sensor noise, motion blur, and loss of detail.

00:00:27.876 --> 00:00:32.396
A camera may brighten a scene automatically while reducing sharpness or color reliability.

00:00:32.396 --> 00:00:36.545
Navigation and obstacle sensors may also have environmental limits that differ from the

00:00:36.545 --> 00:00:37.185
main camera.

00:00:37.185 --> 00:00:41.164
Night operations may have additional legal, lighting, training, and risk requirements.

00:00:41.164 --> 00:00:44.464
Operators should check current official rules and equipment guidance.

00:00:44.464 --> 00:00:48.763
Darkness does not justify reliance on a video feed or automation beyond its documented

00:00:48.763 --> 00:00:49.468
capability.

00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:52.543
Plan camera orientation, exposure behavior, route direction,

00:00:52.543 --> 00:00:54.553
and observation time around the mission.

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:58.192
Avoid sudden movements, use stable capture, and review a sample when safe.

00:00:58.192 --> 00:01:00.802
If glare or shadow blocks the required evidence,

00:01:00.802 --> 00:01:03.221
reschedule or change an authorized viewpoint.

00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:05.121
Image quality is operational quality.

00:01:05.121 --> 00:01:08.591
Clear footage supports analysis, but no image removes uncertainty.

00:01:08.591 --> 00:01:13.510
Document lighting limitations and do not infer detail that the sensor did not reliably

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:13.520
capture.
